This component will be used to upload an image to a server, but first, we need to convert the image to base64 format.

```javascript
import React, { useState } from'react';

function ImageUploadBase64() {
    const [selectedImage, setSelectedImage] = useState(null);
    const [base64Image, setBase64Image] = useState(null);

    const handleImageChange = (event) => {
        setSelectedImage(event.target.files[0]);
        const reader = new FileReader();
        reader.onload = (e) => {
            const dataURL = e.target.result;
            const base64String = dataURL.replace(/^data:image\/(png|jpg);base64,/, "");
            setBase64Image(base64String);
        };
        reader.readAsDataURL(event.target.files[0]);
    };

    return (
        <div>
            <input type="file" onChange={handleImageChange} />
            {base64Image && (
                <div>
                    <p>Base64 Image:</p>
                    <p>{base64Image}</p>
                </div>
            )}
        </div>
    );
}

export default ImageUploadBase64;
```

This component uses the `useState` hook to store the selected image and the base64 image. The `handleImageChange` function is called when the user selects an image. It uses the `FileReader` API to read the selected image and convert it to base64 format. The base64 image is then stored in the component's state. The base64 image is displayed below the input field. 

